1795185635231234	sippycup-2u2m2v	itc:AQ		item.update	bn-1w3	{"field":"title","value":"A signal sent to playpen's whole process group reaches the command twice (outside a new session)"}	blake3:wK_xCgWFWQEGf08vTild1Q_DCrUT_FdYvc026bh2V40
1795185635271543	sippycup-2u2m2v	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-1w3	{"body":"2026-11-20 partly fixed. Reproduced with a counting probe: 5 x kill -USR1 -PGID gave 13 deliveries (normal) and 10 (--new-session); 5 x signalling each playpen process (killall playpen) gave 7. Root cause: three copies. (1) the kernel's own copy to the command when it is in the group; (2) P forwarded with kill(init), and (3) I, which is in P's group, received the group/killall copy itself and forwarded that too; I could not tell (2) from (3), both show as SI_USER from pid 0. Fix: P now names the signal to I as a byte on the existing pipe; I passes on only those, the terminal's (new session), and signals sent to PID 1 from inside the namespace (ssi_pid != 0). Result: to playpen alone 1; killall 1; group in a new session 1; group otherwise 2 (was 2-3). Test a_signal_for_playpen_reaches_the_command_once. LEFT OPEN: outside a new session the command is in P's process group and gets the kernel's copy as well as P's. Neither P nor I can learn whether the command received it: siginfo does not say whether a signal was sent to a pid or a group, and any witness process (in or out of the group) is fooled by per-pid kills that hit the helpers and not the command (killall, pkill -f, kill P I); guessing wrong there loses a SIGTERM, which is worse than a duplicate. Options: (a) accept twice [current]; (b) witness heuristic: skip P's copy when a helper in the group also got one and a second helper outside the group did not: loses the signal for a hand-made 'kill P I', one more process; (c) run the command in its own process group and hand it the terminal (tcsetpgrp): exact, but Ctrl-Z then no longer reaches P and the freeze design has to change; (d) always use --new-session: exact today, costs /dev/tty and job control inside."}	blake3:AgxA3GNf4McgMbaZGgFdqUqUEQvdTHju2uEVU57_afs
