1795199350596663	codex	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-yly	{"description":"Integrate the expected policy and typed readback comparator from bn-1c6 into setup before GO. On supported Linux run the normal CLI with an empty and a nonempty policy and inspect a real nft JSON dump. With a disposable test adapter supplying a harmless narrower readback, assert setup refusal and absence of a workload marker. Preserve existing load failures, cleanup and timeouts. Add the supported nft forms and trust boundary to docs/spec.md startup and docs/DESIGN.md. Capture tool/kernel versions with the results.","kind":"task","labels":["correctness","ruleset"],"parent":"bn-no8","size":"m","title":"Gate workload start on semantic nft readback in a real namespace"}	blake3:G3dk6q8oqh-tEgYlpYztNeR72wz7E_gO2XubLWfDBRQ
1795199350789198	codex	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1ms	{"description":"Use tests/pass.rs and existing CLI supervision tests to map the timing decisions in bn-1th to native behavior. Run a valid pass, expiry, atomic revocation around startup and graceful/forced termination using harmless marker commands. Synchronize on observable readiness when available. Distinguish wall-clock expiry, poll interval, termination signal and process exit. Avoid assertions about a fixed upper bound without scheduling assumptions. Align README, docs/spec.md and docs/DESIGN.md with the observed outcomes and the model's assumptions.","kind":"task","labels":["correctness","revocation"],"parent":"bn-3bg","size":"m","title":"Exercise revocation and expiry through the CLI and reconcile the timing promise"}	blake3:aSnBAtvq01zn6p91PXSj8MNATJYU3Pf7yH4Nfp6gpX4
