1795199392050734	codex	itc:AQ		item.update	bn-k0v	{"field":"description","value":"For a fixed, valid pass and evaluation time, every packet tuple admitted by a selected subset of labels must also be admissible under the full pass's packet-level scope. At b9a0455 pass::load selects destinations before conversion, while approval::excluded_addrs depends on the collection of rules. The pinned Hallpass decision implementation is an independent reference for the full-pass address exclusions. This interaction deserves a direct check.\n\nBuild an in-memory decision oracle from the full pass and compare it with the actual selection and conversion path. Enumerate every subset of small generated passes with overlapping and disjoint scopes, duplicate semantics, both families, boundary addresses, and intersecting port/protocol grants. Include permitted and denied witnesses. Document fixed sandbox exceptions and which application-layer fields fall outside this comparison. Use a stricter synthetic full-pass fixture to check that the inclusion assertion can fail. Preserve any discovered disagreement as a regression and resolve it against the documented contract.\n\nKeep the first check finite and reproducible: exhaust subsets of a documented small pass universe, retain the shortest disagreement, and report which address and port partitions were exercised. An unresolved disagreement needs an explicit contract decision or linked fix before claiming inclusion. The operator-facing policy test consumes production semantics separately."}	blake3:tyYVluDlZth_GvxbYSlJdHtTBIE-pDFO71zTLcZw4Zk
