1795208221492931	lead	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-1w3	{"body":"Release build 17ed1c7, four SIGUSR1 sends spaced 200 ms after child readiness. Supervisor PID and process-group targeting yielded 4 and 8 deliveries in default mode, and 4 and 4 with --new-session. All four commands exited 0. Independent private PTY spike placed the child in its own foreground group. Ctrl-Z stopped the child (SIGTSTP), while the supervisor received zero Ctrl-Z signals, so the existing supervisor-driven whole-sandbox freeze cannot rely on the terminal reaching it after a handoff. A redesign must relay foreground stops and preserve shell fg/bg, nested jobs and foreground pipelines. The existing automated shared-group assertion accepts counts 4 through 8. This remains a live bug."}	blake3:J4aJh6A-4gh6h8FhH2AvsIzhsIpWD3t6Tk9LV7108bI
