1795382350745025	lead	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-1w3	{"body":"Headless portion implemented and verified. Without a controlling terminal, four paced SIGUSR1 sends to P, its group, and individually to the helpers each yielded exactly four receipts. A background workload member and a command that created its own session also received four. The real-terminal default preserves pipeline input, redirected /dev/tty, nested shells and fg/bg. The release binary still recorded eight receipts from four externally generated group sends on an attached private PTY, and four with --new-session. Signals to the attached supervisor PID were single. Keep the attached shared-group case open. The separate foreground-group experiment displaced the outer pipeline, and moving the supervisor out broke shell waitpid(-pgid). The private PTY relay experiment did not preserve redirected stdin plus explicit tty reads without competing for pipeline input. 174 selected tests and all 11 host qualification scenarios passed."}	blake3:vi4zp0SiJHpW529rm3LMxGfXQJpW3ZyG5PqXMjQwtjk
