1795406080392361	playpen-dev	itc:AQ		item.assign	bn-i89	{"action":"assign","agent":"playpen-dev"}	blake3:l51Q-fSmEcf9Nul22iG--Hccp3hro8z1qqyp35B3Q0c
1795407474780794	playpen-dev	itc:AQ		item.move	bn-2ja	{"state":"done"}	blake3:IgMAwC__D9XTjy6PJ8UFqjDqQ8VYnNey3rNGi2-zmfM
1795408416416312	playpen-dev	itc:AQ		item.move	bn-2h7	{"state":"done"}	blake3:YsoO0BDow38lyQ0Zu0uDGJmk5JbFywc_iWW_PwYdGxQ
1795408609216651	playpen-dev	itc:AQ		item.move	bn-bcd	{"state":"done"}	blake3:pFHtLrgMh0b7fw5fF462KitPxHN7Gc2x26CXnqnuv0k
1795409269556811	playpen-dev	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-eby	{"description":"Follow-up to bn-i89 (its recommendation). Decision needed from the owner before building: step 2 has playpen itself load the `vsock` module once per boot when it is not loaded, which changes the host's module set. Without that step a sandbox whose namespace exists when the module is loaded later stays `global`.\n\nEvidence. bn-i89 (docs/DESIGN.md \"Socket families\") measured that in the default `global` VSOCK mode the command reaches the hypervisor host from a VM, and the machine's VMs and vsock listeners from a host, also by acting as a VM through /dev/vhost-vsock (mode 0666 by systemd's udev rules). With ns_mode=local every path failed (ENETUNREACH / ECONNRESET / ENODEV / RST) on 7.1.4 and 7.2.8. An unprivileged route to `local` was shown as uid 1000: unshare --user --map-root-user --net, write `local` to child_ns_mode, then unshare --net.\n\nFirst slice.\n1. In the user namespace playpen creates, make an intermediate network namespace and write `local` to its /proc/sys/net/vsock/child_ns_mode. Then create the sandbox's network namespace inside it with unshare(CLONE_NEWNET), and put the nft table, pasta and the command there. If the write fails with EPERM, the parent is already local; verify by reading ns_mode.\n2. If /proc/sys/net/vsock is absent, first create and close one AF_VSOCK socket so `vsock` is loaded before any sandbox namespace exists; a namespace that exists at load time is global. If AF_VSOCK still cannot be created, record \"unavailable\". On kernels before 7.0 (socket works but there are no sysctls), record \"not confined\" and point to `--hide /dev/vhost-vsock`.\n3. Read ns_mode inside the sandbox and report it: a report field (for example `vsock: \"local\" | \"global\" | \"unavailable\"`), a start-line clause, and a doctor check.\n4. Tests using tests/socket_families.py: ns_mode reads `local` inside the sandbox; a uid-1000 `vsock-listen` in the caller's namespace is not reachable by `vsock-connect 1 PORT` from inside (ECONNRESET, where it connects without the change). These load vsock on the test host; skip with a message where it is not loadable.\n5. Update the README threat model, spec section 8 and DESIGN.md.\n\nOut of scope. Module autoload in general (it needs a seccomp family filter; decide that separately).","kind":"task","labels":["correctness","isolation","follow-up"],"size":"m","title":"Create the sandbox's network namespace in VSOCK local mode and report whether VM sockets are confined"}	blake3:ZjhYFon9MEgOTZg2slwy_0XhdBvVdqM-Sxp0A7V4Dnw
1795409279339323	playpen-dev	itc:AQ		item.move	bn-i89	{"reason":"Recommendation: create the sandbox network namespace in VSOCK local mode and report the VSOCK state (doctor, start line, report). Evidence and table in docs/DESIGN.md 'Socket families'. Follow-up: bn-eby (needs an owner decision on loading the vsock module).","state":"done"}	blake3:WNZ-06HsMoNqetIx9BlNmHCBk8X-uTiM7KXCUw3ZS3I
