1795465392213347	playpen-dev	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2xc	{"description":"Seen on 2026-11-23 while merging bn-r5m and bn-e3h. Neither change touches this code.\n\nEvidence.\n- tests/terminal.rs `private_tty_restores_mode_when_session_leader_is_killed` failed once in a full-suite run on main 1b941e0. The terminal mode was not restored within the test's 2 s after the session leader was killed. It passed 10 of 10 alone and in every later full run.\n- tests/terminal.rs `private_tty_resizes_and_restores_the_outer_terminal_after_interrupt` failed once in 20 under 80 busy loops: no prompt came back after Ctrl-C. It passed 200 of 200 alone, and 40 of 40 parallel suites with and without the bn-e3h fix. The relay's own comment admits a 20 ms polling race around the outer terminal's ISIG switch.\n\nFirst slice. Reproduce each under load (full suite plus busy loops, as bn-1c8 did for the pipeline flake). Find whether the race is in the test (an expectation order, a fixed sleep, a too-short bound) or in the relay (src/terminal_relay.rs polling). Fix the cause; widen a bound only when the bound itself is the cause, and say so.\n\nAcceptance. Each test passes 100 of 100 under load from a workspace path.","kind":"task","labels":["tests","flaky","terminal"],"size":"s","title":"Find why two private-tty tests fail about once in 20 runs under load"}	blake3:t0sLyTgcfBXbUyrveWiad8w8sSkb5S6Tj7uVQCUfSUk
